
			    BBS Modifier v1.0
			   -------------------
               Written on July 13 / 1992   (c) 1992 Ken Rastin


Have you ever gotten sick of always modifying your BBSTEXT file whenever
a new version of Cnet is released? (or a minor upgrade)  This is a quick
program that I threw together to help save some of those headaches.

BBS Modifier v1.0 will modify your new BBSTEXT file according to what your
old one was from the old version of Cnet.  This will save many hours of
work and make you more willing to make those minor updates that are released.

This program is CLI based.  Simply type BBSMOD from your CLI and it will take
things from there.

The program will look for (and will not function without) the following files:

cnet:bbstextnew
cnet:bbstextold
cnet:bbstextmod

cnet:bbstextnew
---------------
This file is the new BBSTEXT file that you are going to be using from now
on. (from the latest version of Cnet that you will be running)


cnet:bbstextold
---------------
This is the original unmodified BBSTEXT file that you are upgrading from. For
the program to work, this should be untouched.


cnet:bbstextmod
---------------
This is the modified BBSTEXT file that you are upgrading from.  These are the
changes that you wish to have included into the new BBSTEXT file.


How does this program work?

  Well it simply compares the 2 files BBSTEXTNEW and BBSTEXTOLD.  It will
compare them line by line and if the line is the same, it will copy over the
the matching line from BBSTEXTMOD. (your modified line)  If the line is
different then that means Ken changed the lines in the new version and they
could mean something else, thus the line from the BBSTEXTNEW is copied over.
(which you may have to modify later).
  The final modifed version will be called BBSTEXT2.  You can rename this as
BBSTEXT to use with your BBS.

Any lines that are not the same are stored in the file called cnet:update
This will include the line number, followed by the line in the BBSTEXTNEW and
finally by the line in the BBSTEXTOLD file.  That way you can quickly look
up anything that the program was unable to modify.

NOTICE:  I can take no responsibility if this program some how fouls up.  I
	 tested it and things seem to run well.  However if problems arise
	 then I hope you made a backup before using it. (MAKE A BACKUP!!)

Now, with that out of the way.  If you want any updates or want to see other
programs that I have written then call:

NOTE:  On the odd occasion the program appends 1-3 garbage lines at the end
of your final BBSTEXT2 file.  When the program is done just check the file
and see if any garbage was appended.  If so, then delete it.  (I am not 
quite sure why it does it, but it is not a major problem as I am sure you
can see)

